  "goodToKnow": "Das Abteil is a train compartment, usually six seats behind a sliding door. Many German trains now have open-plan Großraumwagen, though ICEs often still have some Abteile. The Ruhebereich (quiet zone) asks passengers not to make phone calls. Night trains have Schlafwagenabteile and Liegewagen (couchettes). From abteilen (to partition), related to die Abteilung (department). Plural: die Abteile."
